    "result_text": "I agree with the finding and addressed it. The email-presence predicate was duplicated verbatim in `toContactPreference` and `toMembershipLevel`.\n\nI extracted it into a single `hasEmail(owner)` helper and rewired both call sites:\n- `toContactPreference` \u2192 `return hasEmail(owner) ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";`\n- `toMembershipLevel` \u2192 `if (hasEmail(owner))`\n\nNow the \"is an email present\" rule lives in one place, so any future refinement (e.g. trimming whitespace) can't drift between the two derivations.\n\nTests remain green: full `mvn test` is **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 both acceptance cases (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) still pass.",
