    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe new `toContactPreference` follows the established pattern well \u2014 a `default` helper per derived field, invoked from an `@Mapping` expression, placed alongside the peers, with a matching Javadoc and an `openapi.yml` schema entry. That part is clean and additive.\n\nThe one structural issue is duplicated logic. The email-presence predicate is now written verbatim in two places:\n\n- `toContactPreference` (line 40): `owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty()`\n- `toMembershipLevel` (line 51): the identical expression, assigned to the same `hasEmail` local.\n\nBoth methods encode the same concept (\"does this owner have an email\"), and it's now copy-pasted. Extract it into a single small helper and call it from both:\n\n```java\ndefault boolean hasEmail(Owner owner) {\n    return owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isEmpty();\n}\n```\n\nThen `toContactPreference` becomes `return hasEmail(owner) ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";` and `toMembershipLevel` uses `if (hasEmail(owner))`. This keeps the \"is an email present\" rule in one unit, so a future change to what counts as a present email (e.g. trimming whitespace) can't drift between the two derivations.",
